1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:12,333
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:40,733
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:43,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,500
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,633 --> 00:00:56,967
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,767 --> 00:00:59,567
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:00,800
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:02,333
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,467 --> 00:01:04,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:07,800
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:10,333 --> 00:01:11,633
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:17,267
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,233
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,367 --> 00:01:22,000
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,133 --> 00:01:25,000
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:28,600
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:31,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:34,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,433 --> 00:01:36,367
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:37,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:38,967
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:40,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:46,367 --> 00:01:48,633
<i>There's a huge transaction
going on inside.</i>

24
00:01:48,767 --> 00:01:51,033
<i>I'll find a way
to capture Tiger.</i>

25
00:01:51,733 --> 00:01:53,033
<i>- Excuse me.
- Hey!</i>

26
00:01:53,167 --> 00:01:55,033
<i>- Ow!
- You again?!</i>

27
00:01:55,167 --> 00:01:56,300
<i> Are you stalking me?!</i>

28
00:01:56,433 --> 00:01:58,733
<i>It was you who violated me!
Didn't you kiss me?!</i>

29
00:01:58,867 --> 00:02:00,067
<i> Scumbag!</i>

30
00:02:01,467 --> 00:02:03,067
<i>- Gabo!
- Gabo!</i>

31
00:02:05,567 --> 00:02:07,700
<i> Don't you know that I'm NCIA?</i>

32
00:02:07,833 --> 00:02:10,500
<i>This is the NCIA!
Victor Zafra, hands in the air!</i>

33
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:13,800
<i>- Get in!
- We have to return to Victor!</i>

34
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:16,733
<i>Don't you trust your brother?
He can handle that.</i>

35
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:18,667
<i>- Team.
- Sam?</i>

36
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,000
<i>I'll follow Tiger.
Follow his men!</i>

37
00:02:21,133 --> 00:02:22,067
<i> Copy.</i>

38
00:02:45,367 --> 00:02:46,367
<i> What do you want from me?!</i>

39
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:48,767
<i>A huge bounty's been placed
on your head</i>

40
00:02:48,933 --> 00:02:50,700
<i>for ruining the lives
of countless people.</i>

41
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:52,367
You deserve to rot behind bars!

42
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,467
<i> You think you can escape?!</i>

43
00:02:57,533 --> 00:02:58,533
<i> Stop!</i>

44
00:02:59,133 --> 00:03:00,333
<i> You can't catch me!</i>

45
00:03:03,333 --> 00:03:04,967
[TIRES SCREECHING]

46
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:07,967
[GABO] You psycho!
You can't escape!

47
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:09,933
[SEBASTIAN] Team, apprehend
the suspects! Move!

48
00:03:10,067 --> 00:03:13,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:03:13,267 --> 00:03:14,200
Jacinto!

50
00:03:15,067 --> 00:03:17,033
[HOSE WHIPS, CREAKS]

51
00:03:17,167 --> 00:03:20,400
[GABO] Ahh! Ahh!

52
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:22,833
[HOSE WHIRRING]

53
00:03:24,667 --> 00:03:27,233
[VICTOR GROANING]

54
00:03:27,367 --> 00:03:28,700
- [HOSE WHIRRING]
- [ROOF CLANGS]

55
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:30,400
[VICTOR GROANING]

56
00:03:30,533 --> 00:03:31,433
[SAM] Stop!

57
00:03:31,567 --> 00:03:35,000
[GUNSHOTS]

58
00:03:39,067 --> 00:03:41,367
Victor Zafra,
you're under arrest.

59
00:03:43,033 --> 00:03:44,567
- Cuff him.
- [SEBASTIAN] Get up!

60
00:03:48,233 --> 00:03:50,833
There goes our money.

61
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:57,233
[HANDCUFFS RATTLING]

62
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,700
[SEBASTIAN] Alright, walk.

63
00:04:01,033 --> 00:04:02,833
[SAM] Castor, Rallos,
someone escaped.

64
00:04:02,967 --> 00:04:04,067
<i> Can you track him?</i>

65
00:04:05,333 --> 00:04:06,933
[DIGITAL BEEPING]

66
00:04:07,067 --> 00:04:09,467
[TONY] Positive. Unidentified
subject moving eastbound.

67
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:10,867
<i>All units,
intercept the subject.</i>

68
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,400
<i> Don't let him get away.</i>

69
00:04:13,233 --> 00:04:15,467
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [FOOTSTEPS]

70
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:16,533
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am!

71
00:04:16,667 --> 00:04:18,600
Stay on the target.
We're losing signal.

72
00:04:18,733 --> 00:04:21,000
[MAN]<i> All units, a man's running
</i> in the parking lot.

73
00:04:21,133 --> 00:04:23,267
- Catch him! No one can escape!
- [GUNSHOTS]

74
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:25,667
<i>- Don't let him escape!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

75
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,733
[CARS THUDDING]

76
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:29,733
[MAN] Hey, you!
Stop right there!

77
00:04:32,733 --> 00:04:33,867
[LOUD CRASH]

78
00:04:35,133 --> 00:04:36,133
[GUNSHOT]

79
00:04:38,533 --> 00:04:40,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

80
00:04:40,733 --> 00:04:44,767
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

81
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:46,367
[GATE SHATTERS]

82
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:48,800
[GUNSHOTS]

83
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,000
[GUNSHOT]

84
00:04:51,133 --> 00:04:56,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

85
00:04:57,067 --> 00:04:58,033
[GUNSHOTS]

86
00:05:01,133 --> 00:05:02,600
[GLASS SHATTERS]

87
00:05:04,167 --> 00:05:06,033
[WOOD CLATTERS]

88
00:05:06,167 --> 00:05:07,233
[THUDS]

89
00:05:07,367 --> 00:05:08,933
[PLASTIC RUSTLING]

90
00:05:09,067 --> 00:05:10,933
- [METAL CLANKS]
- [THUDS]

91
00:05:11,067 --> 00:05:12,700
[TRUCK HORN BLARING]

92
00:05:12,833 --> 00:05:18,367
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

93
00:05:18,733 --> 00:05:24,167
[CAR APPROACHES]

94
00:05:26,667 --> 00:05:29,833
[DOOR CLICKS]

95
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,333
[DOOR SLAMS]

96
00:05:33,467 --> 00:05:40,467
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

97
00:05:41,833 --> 00:05:43,000
What happened?

98
00:05:43,667 --> 00:05:44,900
Where's Victor?

99
00:05:45,367 --> 00:05:46,200
[ARTURO] Sir.

100
00:05:46,333 --> 00:05:47,567
The police arrived.

101
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:48,933
There was a shootout.

102
00:05:49,067 --> 00:05:50,867
But where is Victor?!

103
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,033
[LUCAS] Papa.

104
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:54,167
We got separated

105
00:05:54,567 --> 00:05:55,767
in the middle of the shootout.

106
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,933
[LEE] But Sir Victor called me.

107
00:05:58,333 --> 00:05:59,767
I already sent backup.

108
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:02,600
[ARTURO] Sir,
our men will protect him.

109
00:06:02,733 --> 00:06:04,400
[DEBORAH] What about
his other deal?

110
00:06:04,533 --> 00:06:06,767
What about the gold bars
he's carrying?

111
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:13,867
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

112
00:06:19,333 --> 00:06:21,100
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

113
00:06:21,233 --> 00:06:22,533
Let me go!

114
00:06:23,933 --> 00:06:24,967
Didn't you hear what I said?!

115
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:28,033
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

116
00:06:28,167 --> 00:06:33,100
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

117
00:06:33,233 --> 00:06:34,567
Bring him upstairs.

118
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:36,800
[TONY] Move it.

119
00:06:40,367 --> 00:06:41,900
[DELGADO] Good job, team.
Good job.

120
00:06:42,067 --> 00:06:47,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

121
00:06:47,667 --> 00:06:49,533
Well done, Sam. Well done.

122
00:06:49,667 --> 00:06:51,367
- Thank you, Chief.
- [DELGADO CHUCKLES]

123
00:06:52,900 --> 00:06:54,300
[CHUCKLES]

124
00:06:54,433 --> 00:06:55,567
You'll just shake my hand?

125
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:58,800
[TENDER, EMOTIONAL
MUSIC PLAYING]

126
00:06:58,933 --> 00:07:00,233
[CHUCKLES]

127
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,433
Chief, thank you
for trusting me.

128
00:07:07,267 --> 00:07:08,900
But I just want
to remind you

129
00:07:09,033 --> 00:07:10,967
that I didn't catch
Victor Zafra alone.

130
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:14,000
I know, I know.

131
00:07:14,167 --> 00:07:18,467
You worked as a group,
but you are their leader.

132
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:20,433
You lead this operation.

133
00:07:20,567 --> 00:07:22,967
Don't discredit yourself.

134
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,767
You are amazing.

135
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:28,900
And I am proud of you.

136
00:07:31,067 --> 00:07:33,233
Hey, we still have
a press conference upstairs.

137
00:07:33,367 --> 00:07:40,367
[TENDER, EMOTIONAL
MUSIC CONTINUES PLAYING]

138
00:07:41,567 --> 00:07:42,867
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]
- [CAMERA CLICKS]

139
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,567
[REPORTER 1] Victor Zafra,
what can you say

140
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:46,200
about the allegations
against you?

141
00:07:46,333 --> 00:07:47,433
Victor Zafra,

142
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,333
- what can you say about this?
- [REPORTER 2] Sir! Sir!

143
00:07:49,467 --> 00:07:50,800
Could you please explain
what's going on?

144
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:53,100
Good evening, everyone.

145
00:07:55,533 --> 00:07:58,367
A big fish was caught.

146
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:02,100
He's the leader
of the gold smuggling syndicate.

147
00:08:02,233 --> 00:08:03,833
Victor Zafra.

148
00:08:03,967 --> 00:08:05,400
Aslo knows as Tiger.

149
00:08:06,933 --> 00:08:10,767
The abuse of our natural
resources and the theft

150
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:13,833
from our country
will finally stop

151
00:08:13,967 --> 00:08:16,567
because he has been caught.

152
00:08:17,233 --> 00:08:19,200
And tonight,
I am proud to say

153
00:08:19,333 --> 00:08:23,600
that his capture would not
have been possible

154
00:08:23,767 --> 00:08:29,267
if not for the NCIA agents
led by Sam Jacinto.

155
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:31,200
Sam Jacinto.

156
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:34,167
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]
- Yes?

157
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:36,500
How did you catch
Victor Zafra?

158
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,100
Jacinto, answer the question.

159
00:08:40,367 --> 00:08:42,400
We monitored his every move.

160
00:08:42,533 --> 00:08:44,733
We discovered that they had
a transaction tonight,

161
00:08:44,867 --> 00:08:47,000
so we took the opportunity
to catch him.

162
00:08:47,133 --> 00:08:50,633
Are there any other arrests
related to this case?

163
00:08:50,767 --> 00:08:52,200
How big is their network?

164
00:08:52,333 --> 00:08:54,333
Our investigation
is still ongoing,

165
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,133
so there are still so many
unanswered questions.

166
00:08:56,267 --> 00:08:57,733
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

167
00:08:57,867 --> 00:08:59,867
[DELGADO] What's important
is that...

168
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:05,467
this is one of NCIA's greatest
achievements up to date!

169
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,633
Capturing the man we've
been pursuing for a long time,

170
00:09:07,767 --> 00:09:09,300
Victor Zafra.

171
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,467
also known as Tiger.

172
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:13,500
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]
- Thank you.

173
00:09:14,033 --> 00:09:16,767
[REPORTER 1] Sir, we still have
some questions!

174
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:19,800
Sir, what are your
plans for him?

175
00:09:19,933 --> 00:09:25,133
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

176
00:09:25,267 --> 00:09:32,267
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

177
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:37,933
[LAWIN] Gabo.

178
00:09:45,733 --> 00:09:46,933
[GUN CLICKS]

179
00:09:47,067 --> 00:09:49,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

180
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:52,167
[DOOR OPENS]

181
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:59,767
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

182
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:05,267
You'll now pay
for all your crimes.

183
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:07,467
You'll rot in jail.

184
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:09,967
[CLEARS THROAT]

185
00:10:10,333 --> 00:10:11,500
You guys are arrogant.

186
00:10:11,967 --> 00:10:12,967
You just got lucky.

187
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:15,067
It's all because of the guy
who was chasing me.

188
00:10:16,633 --> 00:10:18,067
A man chasing you?

189
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:26,200
You were so proud
in front of the press.

190
00:10:26,333 --> 00:10:28,400
One of your men wasn't even
the one who tackled me.

191
00:10:29,333 --> 00:10:30,200
[INHALES]

192
00:10:30,333 --> 00:10:31,300
Fine.

193
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:33,167
Tell us who that man is.

194
00:10:33,533 --> 00:10:34,967
What does he have to do
with your group?

195
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:37,733
Why don't you investigate him
yourself? You're good, right?

196
00:10:38,967 --> 00:10:39,900
Jacinto.

197
00:10:40,233 --> 00:10:42,200
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

198
00:10:46,133 --> 00:10:47,933
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

199
00:10:48,067 --> 00:10:55,000
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

200
00:11:00,933 --> 00:11:03,600
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

201
00:11:03,733 --> 00:11:04,700
Gabo.

202
00:11:05,367 --> 00:11:06,433
What happened?

203
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:08,833
Where is Tiger?

204
00:11:10,967 --> 00:11:12,133
Tiger got away.

205
00:11:12,767 --> 00:11:13,933
But I caught him.

206
00:11:14,267 --> 00:11:16,333
But someone came
and fired shots at me!

207
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:19,533
Get in.

208
00:11:22,967 --> 00:11:23,867
Get in.

209
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,133
Get inside.

210
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:35,833
[CHAIR DRAGS]

211
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,633
Sit.

212
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:43,067
[MUSIC TURNS PENSIVE]

213
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:49,267
[CLEARS THROAT]

214
00:11:51,733 --> 00:11:52,900
Good evening, sir.

215
00:11:53,433 --> 00:11:55,867
Miss, give me your specialty.

216
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,300
Stir-fried noodles,

217
00:11:57,867 --> 00:11:59,533
special fried chicken and...

218
00:12:00,333 --> 00:12:01,367
spring rolls, please.

219
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:04,467
Two beers.

220
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:07,367
- Wait.
- [WAITRESS] Okay.

221
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:09,767
Just good for two, okay?
Thank you.

222
00:12:13,467 --> 00:12:14,467
Gabo.

223
00:12:15,833 --> 00:12:16,933
What happened?

224
00:12:19,033 --> 00:12:19,900
Where's Tiger?

225
00:12:20,033 --> 00:12:23,000
Pops had high expectations
of you.

226
00:12:23,733 --> 00:12:25,833
You know how big of a deal
this mission is.

227
00:12:26,367 --> 00:12:27,500
And you wasted it.

228
00:12:27,633 --> 00:12:30,200
Gabo, we really thought

229
00:12:30,567 --> 00:12:33,200
this mission
would be easy for you.

230
00:12:35,233 --> 00:12:36,600
But you have failed us.

231
00:12:37,067 --> 00:12:38,400
[GABO] I got hold of Tiger.

232
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:40,400
I even beat up his people.

233
00:12:41,667 --> 00:12:43,033
But someone suddenly showed up.

234
00:12:44,033 --> 00:12:45,267
They fired shots at me.

235
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,467
That's when Tiger got away.

236
00:12:47,867 --> 00:12:50,033
[UWAK] You know your mission.

237
00:12:50,533 --> 00:12:53,467
To catch Tiger dead or alive.

238
00:12:53,967 --> 00:12:56,633
You've failed us
on your first mission, Gabo.

239
00:12:58,433 --> 00:12:59,700
What does that mean?

240
00:13:01,967 --> 00:13:02,933
Where's my money?

241
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:05,833
How will you get your money

242
00:13:05,967 --> 00:13:07,700
now that you failed
on your mission?

243
00:13:07,833 --> 00:13:08,800
[LAWIN] Gabo.

244
00:13:08,933 --> 00:13:10,233
Our deal was clear.

245
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:13,900
You'll bring Tiger's head
to Pops.

246
00:13:14,567 --> 00:13:16,267
Once that's done,
you'll get paid.

247
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:18,733
But you're going to get, so...

248
00:13:19,233 --> 00:13:20,533
you're not getting paid.

249
00:13:20,667 --> 00:13:21,967
Son of a gun.

250
00:13:23,633 --> 00:13:24,967
You think this is a joke to me?

251
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:27,333
I risked my life out there!

252
00:13:28,167 --> 00:13:30,167
That was tiring! Now you're
telling me I won't get paid?!

253
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:31,967
You failed to do your mission.

254
00:13:33,433 --> 00:13:34,633
You're not getting paid.

255
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:40,267
I desperately need
the money right now.

256
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:42,733
My father is in the hospital.

257
00:13:43,033 --> 00:13:44,433
He needs surgery!

258
00:13:44,567 --> 00:13:45,733
[LAWIN] Oh, no, no, no.

259
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:48,733
As much as we want to help,
there's nothing we can do.

260
00:13:48,967 --> 00:13:50,400
You failed on your mission,

261
00:13:51,633 --> 00:13:52,733
you're not getting any money.

262
00:13:52,867 --> 00:13:59,800
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

263
00:14:01,367 --> 00:14:03,233
What was Zafra saying?

264
00:14:04,233 --> 00:14:05,867
Who was the man
he was talking about?

265
00:14:06,733 --> 00:14:08,833
Sir, that's exactly what
I wanted to tell you earlier.

266
00:14:09,233 --> 00:14:11,533
A man suddenly appeared
while we were on the mission.

267
00:14:12,133 --> 00:14:14,400
I think he's one
of Zaffra's enemies as well.

268
00:14:14,767 --> 00:14:17,167
You need to find out
who that man is.

269
00:14:18,133 --> 00:14:19,767
Okay. I'll investigate it.

270
00:14:20,433 --> 00:14:23,167
What matters now is
that the case is solved.

271
00:14:23,567 --> 00:14:26,633
This is a win for NCIA.

272
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:28,500
If someone gets in the way,

273
00:14:28,667 --> 00:14:31,133
whether it be our enemy
or our enemy's enemy,

274
00:14:31,433 --> 00:14:34,067
we must always be prepared.

275
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:41,167
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

276
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:42,533
[BOTTLE CAP CLICKS]

277
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,367
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

278
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:47,333
Arturo,

279
00:14:47,467 --> 00:14:49,500
we've been waiting here
for ages.

280
00:14:50,867 --> 00:14:53,733
Are there any updates
from our people?

281
00:14:54,733 --> 00:14:56,700
Find out if Victor
is on his way here.

282
00:14:56,833 --> 00:14:58,367
Yes, sir. I'll call them again.

283
00:15:00,867 --> 00:15:02,600
Ma'am? Ma'am?

284
00:15:02,767 --> 00:15:03,967
You might want
to check on this.

285
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:11,067
[INDISTINCT CHATTER
OVER SPEAKERS]

286
00:15:11,633 --> 00:15:13,800
[DELGADO OVER SPEAKERS]
<i> Good evening, everyone.</i>

287
00:15:13,933 --> 00:15:17,233
We caught a big fish tonight...

288
00:15:17,367 --> 00:15:20,433
<i>...the leader of the
gold smuggling syndicate,</i>

289
00:15:20,567 --> 00:15:23,800
<i> Victor Zafra, alias "Tiger."</i>

290
00:15:25,567 --> 00:15:27,933
<i>The abuse
on our natural resources,</i>

291
00:15:28,067 --> 00:15:30,867
<i>and the stealing
from our country</i>

292
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:35,200
<i>will stop
because he is now caught.</i>

293
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:38,533
- [TWINKLE] Ma'am, good news!
- Oh, really?

294
00:15:38,667 --> 00:15:41,533
I'm delivering the news to you
right away.

295
00:15:41,667 --> 00:15:42,933
It's still hot!

296
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:48,400
<i> If not for the NCIA agents</i>

297
00:15:48,533 --> 00:15:50,400
<i> led by Sam Jacinto.</i>

298
00:15:52,233 --> 00:15:53,200
[EXHALES]

299
00:15:55,433 --> 00:15:57,233
- [TOTO CHUCKLING]
- Ah!

300
00:15:57,367 --> 00:16:02,200
I'm sure ma'am is the one
who defeated those criminals!

301
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:04,733
[TWINKLE] Ma'am Sam
is so amazing!

302
00:16:04,867 --> 00:16:06,833
She's just like Sir Ricardo!

303
00:16:06,967 --> 00:16:09,900
Her workaholic nature
finally paid off.

304
00:16:10,067 --> 00:16:13,733
We have to show this to Ricardo,

305
00:16:13,867 --> 00:16:16,333
so he can be proud
of his daughter.

306
00:16:16,467 --> 00:16:17,767
- Right?
- Yes!

307
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:20,733
- Come, accompany me.
- Ma'am.

308
00:16:20,867 --> 00:16:23,100
[INDISTINCT CHATTER
OVER SPEAKERS]

309
00:16:23,233 --> 00:16:25,733
[REPORTER]<i> How did
</i> you catch Victor Zafra?

310
00:16:25,867 --> 00:16:27,267
This is your fault.

311
00:16:28,867 --> 00:16:31,933
[BLOWS, KICKS LANDING]

312
00:16:32,067 --> 00:16:33,333
- Lucas!
- Boss, that's enough.

313
00:16:33,467 --> 00:16:35,533
- That's enough, that's enough.
- Let go of me!

314
00:16:35,667 --> 00:16:37,933
- That's enough. That's enough.
- [ARTURO GRUNTS, COUGHS]

315
00:16:38,067 --> 00:16:40,367
This is your fault!
If you didn't pull me,

316
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:41,967
Victor would've been with me!

317
00:16:42,133 --> 00:16:43,833
- He wouldn't have been caught!
- Lucas!

318
00:16:44,533 --> 00:16:45,633
That's enough.

319
00:16:49,900 --> 00:16:53,167
[ISOBEL] Hi, hon!
Look at this!

320
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:55,833
You better watch this.

321
00:16:55,967 --> 00:16:57,967
[SAM OVER PHONE]
<i> We studied his movements.</i>

322
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:00,333
<i>We discovered they have
a transaction tonight,</i>

323
00:17:00,467 --> 00:17:03,033
so we took it as the opportunity
<i> to catch him.</i>

324
00:17:06,667 --> 00:17:08,667
<i>Our investigation
is still ongoing.</i>

325
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:10,100
It's this woman's fault!

326
00:17:10,833 --> 00:17:11,933
Who is she?

327
00:17:12,733 --> 00:17:14,600
She doesn't know
the family she's dealing with.

328
00:17:14,767 --> 00:17:21,733
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

329
00:17:26,367 --> 00:17:28,733
[ISOBEL] Aren't we proud
of our youngest?

330
00:17:28,867 --> 00:17:32,433
Ma'am Sam proved that
she's an exceptional Jacinto!

331
00:17:32,567 --> 00:17:35,200
A huge group
solved one small case.

332
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,400
What's impressive about that?

333
00:17:38,567 --> 00:17:39,567
What?

334
00:17:40,367 --> 00:17:42,100
My god,
what are you talking about?

335
00:17:42,233 --> 00:17:44,500
This isn't a small case!

336
00:17:44,633 --> 00:17:46,067
Well, anyway,
when she gets home,

337
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:50,100
we should all congratulate Sam
for doing a good job.

338
00:17:50,267 --> 00:17:52,700
And please tell her
how proud you are.

339
00:17:52,833 --> 00:17:55,333
Well, don't disturb me.
I have a lot of work to do.

340
00:17:55,467 --> 00:17:57,467
[DELGADO OVER PHONE]
...for catching our most wanted,

341
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:59,067
<i> Victor Zafra.</i>

342
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:06,133
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

343
00:18:15,567 --> 00:18:16,400
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS]

344
00:18:16,533 --> 00:18:18,700
Boss, one of Domingo's men
is outside.

345
00:18:18,833 --> 00:18:20,433
They want us
to fulfill our part.

346
00:18:20,567 --> 00:18:21,633
[PAQUITO SCOFFS]

347
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:27,300
Those cops never miss
when it's about money.

348
00:18:27,867 --> 00:18:29,967
Guess you really can't
outsmart them, huh?

349
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:31,767
The cunning only get richer.

350
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:35,733
You really know how
to make money.

351
00:18:35,867 --> 00:18:37,200
Look, Betchay.

352
00:18:38,133 --> 00:18:43,433
That's why so many are eager
to take my position from me.

353
00:18:43,567 --> 00:18:46,033
Because even the people
around me

354
00:18:46,633 --> 00:18:48,300
are living in paradise.

355
00:18:48,433 --> 00:18:50,167
If we had been together,

356
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:52,767
you would have been
living the life.

357
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:56,233
I'd rather stay poor
than being queen of crime.

358
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:58,700
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

359
00:18:58,833 --> 00:18:59,867
(In Japanese) Cheers!

360
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:00,867
[PAQUITO CHUCKLES]

361
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,867
- Hey, Ibyang.
- What's up?

362
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,367
So, where's the bar's money?

363
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:06,200
- [BETCHAY LAUGHING]
- [BOTTLES CLINK]

364
00:19:06,333 --> 00:19:08,867
Drink up, so we can go for more.

365
00:19:09,733 --> 00:19:11,067
[BETCHAY GIGGLES, EXHALES]

366
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:12,533
Nice and cold.

367
00:19:12,667 --> 00:19:14,200
What's going on here?!

368
00:19:15,033 --> 00:19:16,767
What is this woman doing here?!

369
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:17,900
What else?

370
00:19:18,033 --> 00:19:20,567
She's looking for work,
so I hired her.

371
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:21,733
I'm hired?

372
00:19:21,867 --> 00:19:23,267
- Yes!
- Boss, thank you!

373
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,633
You've really got
some nerve, huh?!

374
00:19:26,167 --> 00:19:27,700
Do you know
what Gabo did to us?!

375
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:28,900
Hang on!

376
00:19:29,067 --> 00:19:30,800
I've got nothing to do
with Gabo!

377
00:19:30,933 --> 00:19:33,933
I'm the one looking
for a job, not him!

378
00:19:34,067 --> 00:19:35,933
Geez, do you see him?

379
00:19:36,067 --> 00:19:37,733
- He's not here!
- You dare talk back!

380
00:19:37,867 --> 00:19:39,800
Of course! Are you my boss?

381
00:19:39,933 --> 00:19:42,400
My husband owns this bar!

382
00:19:42,533 --> 00:19:43,700
That makes me the owner, too!

383
00:19:43,833 --> 00:19:46,200
Our families are enemies,
so why are you here?!

384
00:19:46,333 --> 00:19:48,400
Again, I don't care
about your feud with Gabo!

385
00:19:48,533 --> 00:19:49,867
Why drag me into this?!

386
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,900
- My goodness!
- Hold on, wait!

387
00:19:52,033 --> 00:19:53,700
Don't start a fight here!

388
00:19:53,833 --> 00:19:54,933
That's bad luck for business!

389
00:19:55,067 --> 00:19:57,233
She and her family are bad luck!

390
00:19:57,367 --> 00:19:59,600
Not just for business,
but for my life too!

391
00:20:00,633 --> 00:20:02,500
Betchay, you should go.

392
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:04,500
Just come back another day.

393
00:20:04,633 --> 00:20:06,867
Promise, boss? You hired me.

394
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:07,933
I'm hired.

395
00:20:08,067 --> 00:20:09,133
Scram!

396
00:20:09,267 --> 00:20:11,800
- Stop provoking her!
- Where's my bag?

397
00:20:11,933 --> 00:20:13,033
Give me my bag!

398
00:20:13,167 --> 00:20:14,767
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

399
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:16,233
- Oh?
- You actually hired...

400
00:20:16,367 --> 00:20:18,233
Gabo's mother?

401
00:20:18,367 --> 00:20:19,767
Have you lost your mind?!

402
00:20:21,667 --> 00:20:25,133
Ibyang, I know what I'm doing.

403
00:20:25,733 --> 00:20:26,800
Stay out of this.

404
00:20:26,933 --> 00:20:28,367
Come on, let's go home!

405
00:20:33,733 --> 00:20:40,700
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

406
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:52,833
You, come with me.

407
00:20:52,967 --> 00:20:54,900
The rest of you,
we'll meet there.

408
00:20:55,033 --> 00:20:57,000
We're going to attack
the NCIA tonight

409
00:20:57,133 --> 00:20:58,633
and rescue my son.

410
00:20:58,767 --> 00:20:59,767
Get ready!

411
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:00,967
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

412
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:03,833
[GUNS COCKING]

413
00:21:05,567 --> 00:21:06,833
Hang on, hang on!

414
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:10,167
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

415
00:21:10,333 --> 00:21:11,700
Where are you going?

416
00:21:12,233 --> 00:21:14,267
We're hitting the NCIA.

417
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:16,133
I'm getting my son out.

418
00:21:27,033 --> 00:21:28,567
Are you thinking straight?

419
00:21:29,233 --> 00:21:30,867
Do you think it's that easy?

420
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,667
What do you want me to do?

421
00:21:33,267 --> 00:21:35,633
Let my son rot in prison?

422
00:21:35,767 --> 00:21:39,167
I have spoken to our lawyer.

423
00:21:39,867 --> 00:21:41,733
We will do this the right way.

424
00:21:42,300 --> 00:21:43,700
The legal way.

425
00:21:44,467 --> 00:21:46,733
If you resort to violence,

426
00:21:46,867 --> 00:21:48,400
it will open a can of worms,

427
00:21:48,533 --> 00:21:53,367
and the authorities will target
our organization even more.

428
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:56,033
I'm prepared for anything
that might happen.

429
00:21:56,167 --> 00:21:58,700
The most important thing for me
is break my son out!

430
00:21:58,833 --> 00:22:02,100
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

431
00:22:02,233 --> 00:22:03,967
You might be prepared,

432
00:22:04,933 --> 00:22:06,100
but I am not.

433
00:22:06,233 --> 00:22:12,067
I refuse to watch everything
we have worked hard for collapse

434
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:15,167
just because of your
reckless behavior.

435
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:18,667
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

436
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:21,400
You are not going to the NCIA.

437
00:22:23,333 --> 00:22:24,667
That's an order.

438
00:22:29,033 --> 00:22:30,067
[DEBORAH SIGHS]

439
00:22:31,367 --> 00:22:35,033
Would you trust
my decision on this?

440
00:22:35,700 --> 00:22:37,567
Calm yourself.

441
00:22:37,700 --> 00:22:39,900
I don't want you stressing
yourself out.

442
00:22:40,033 --> 00:22:45,067
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

443
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:46,967
- Arturo!
- Sir.

444
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:48,500
Stand down.

445
00:22:49,067 --> 00:22:50,067
Sir.

446
00:22:51,567 --> 00:22:53,400
[ARTURO] Men, stand down!

447
00:22:54,033 --> 00:22:55,400
[GUNS RATTLING]

448
00:22:56,767 --> 00:22:57,833
Come on.

449
00:22:58,933 --> 00:22:59,867
Let's go.

450
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,133
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

451
00:23:05,933 --> 00:23:07,133
- There you go.
- Perfect.

452
00:23:07,267 --> 00:23:08,967
Boss, Chinatown was
warming with people,

453
00:23:09,100 --> 00:23:10,167
so we hit big over there.

454
00:23:10,300 --> 00:23:12,100
That's exactly what
I like about you guys.

455
00:23:12,233 --> 00:23:14,800
You pull it off smooth, no one
gets caught or dragged down.

456
00:23:14,933 --> 00:23:16,400
- [LAUGHING]
- No phones this time?

457
00:23:16,533 --> 00:23:18,233
You guys delivered,
so here's your cut.

458
00:23:18,367 --> 00:23:19,767
- Wow!
- Split it up fair and square.

459
00:23:19,900 --> 00:23:21,067
- Got it.
- Thanks, boss.

460
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:23,300
- Alright, get moving now.
- Thanks, boss.

461
00:23:25,267 --> 00:23:27,600
[IBYANG] You really are
something else, Paquito!

462
00:23:27,733 --> 00:23:29,167
We're talking
about our enemies...

463
00:23:29,300 --> 00:23:34,100
and you still go hiring them?!
Are you out of your mind?!

464
00:23:34,233 --> 00:23:36,767
Ibyang, there's an old saying...

465
00:23:36,900 --> 00:23:40,033
"If you're not close with
them, bring them close to you!"

466
00:23:40,167 --> 00:23:41,700
That's how it goes!

467
00:23:41,833 --> 00:23:44,200
You talk way too much, and
your logic makes no sense!

468
00:23:44,333 --> 00:23:45,433
What is going on with you guys?

469
00:23:45,567 --> 00:23:47,733
You really had to start a fight
during Chinese New Year?

470
00:23:47,867 --> 00:23:49,767
Well, what do you
expect? Look at your father!

471
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:53,233
He actually gave Betchay
a job over at BeerGin.

472
00:23:53,367 --> 00:23:55,000
Wait... Betchay?

473
00:23:55,167 --> 00:23:56,233
Yeah.

474
00:23:56,367 --> 00:23:57,900
Oh, for crying out loud.

475
00:23:58,033 --> 00:23:59,200
Why would you do that, Pa?

476
00:23:59,333 --> 00:24:03,667
I already explained it to your
mother, but she won't listen!

477
00:24:04,867 --> 00:24:07,167
What's your reason, Pa?

478
00:24:07,300 --> 00:24:09,533
You know I'm the one
who took care of Rudy.

479
00:24:09,667 --> 00:24:11,233
Betchay might find out.

480
00:24:11,367 --> 00:24:13,500
- See what I mean?
- If Gabo hears about this,

481
00:24:13,633 --> 00:24:15,667
we are in deep trouble!

482
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:18,333
Aren't there rumors going around

483
00:24:18,467 --> 00:24:20,967
that Gabo is
building up his crew?

484
00:24:21,100 --> 00:24:22,900
That's why I brought Betchay in.

485
00:24:23,033 --> 00:24:24,900
So if things go south,

486
00:24:25,033 --> 00:24:29,100
we can use her as
leverage against Gabo.

487
00:24:29,267 --> 00:24:30,333
That's why!

488
00:24:30,467 --> 00:24:33,500
So you better listen up.

489
00:24:33,633 --> 00:24:37,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

490
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:39,633
[GRUNTING]

491
00:24:39,767 --> 00:24:41,267
[BOTTLES CLINKING]

492
00:24:49,267 --> 00:24:56,100
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

493
00:24:57,700 --> 00:24:59,833
What's going to happen
to me now?

494
00:25:03,900 --> 00:25:06,633
Just wait for your next mission.

495
00:25:06,767 --> 00:25:08,833
Do a good job.

496
00:25:08,967 --> 00:25:12,200
And whatever you
do, don't let us down.

497
00:25:15,833 --> 00:25:17,767
You guys just
played me for a fool.

498
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:23,400
You set me up
and fed me lies.

499
00:25:24,800 --> 00:25:26,233
You're all full of crap.

500
00:25:26,367 --> 00:25:27,533
[FIST SLAMS TABLE]

501
00:25:27,667 --> 00:25:34,533
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

502
00:25:49,700 --> 00:25:53,333
<i>Find a way to get Victor
out of jail right now.</i>

503
00:25:53,467 --> 00:25:55,067
<i>I know another
way we can do this.</i>

504
00:25:55,200 --> 00:25:56,967
<i> The woman who arrested Victor</i>

505
00:25:57,100 --> 00:25:59,700
<i>is General Ricardo
Jacinto's daughter.</i>

506
00:25:59,833 --> 00:26:01,567
<i>The Zafras are legitimate
business owners.</i>

507
00:26:01,700 --> 00:26:03,500
<i>Maybe you locked up
the wrong guy this time.</i>

508
00:26:03,633 --> 00:26:06,800
<i>The NCIA locked up a
criminal thanks to me.</i>

509
00:26:06,933 --> 00:26:10,200
<i>I believe I did my job
the best way I knew how.</i>

510
00:26:10,367 --> 00:26:11,667
<i>Are you really going
to question me on this?</i>

511
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:13,500
Is that wrong in your eyes too?

512
00:26:13,633 --> 00:26:16,133
<i>For once, forget that
you're a former general.</i>

513
00:26:16,267 --> 00:26:17,267
<i> Just be a father!</i>

514
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:19,700
<i>I'm doing this for
you, to get revenge.</i>

515
00:26:19,833 --> 00:26:22,367
<i>That man is mine.
He's my problem.</i>

516
00:26:22,500 --> 00:26:23,800
<i>Already caught, and
still managed to escape?</i>

517
00:26:23,933 --> 00:26:26,633
<i>I'm sure the cops are the
ones benefiting from this.</i>

518
00:26:26,767 --> 00:26:28,400
<i> You never listen, Sam!</i>

519
00:26:28,533 --> 00:26:31,333
<i>Because you're so
stubborn, our family fell apart!</i>

520
00:26:31,467 --> 00:26:32,767
<i> Let me out of here!</i>

521
00:26:32,900 --> 00:26:34,733
<i>I'm not the one you should
be holding responsible!</i>

522
00:26:34,867 --> 00:26:38,800
<i>That bike is still in
hock because of you.</i>

523
00:26:38,933 --> 00:26:41,167
<i>I was about to pay for it!
I was gonna get it back!</i>

524
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:43,300
<i>Your dad needs that
money for his surgery!</i>

525
00:26:43,467 --> 00:26:44,900
<i> I need to make a move now.</i>

526
00:26:45,033 --> 00:26:47,267
<i>This is the only way for us
to get the cash</i>

527
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:49,300
<i> to pay for Papa's operation.</i>
